    "knowledge_point": "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Parallel To Two Lines",
    "problem": "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $A(7,-2,3)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨9,2,1⟩+s⟨2,-2,1⟩$ and $r=⟨4,-5,19⟩+t⟨3,4,7⟩.$",
    "worked_solution": "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨2,-2,1⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨3,4,7⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $A(7,-2,3)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $a=⟨7,-2,3⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =a+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨7,-2,3⟩+s⟨2,-2,1⟩+t⟨3,4,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
